we have disturbing new surveillance  video from Jersey City New Jersey this  shows the moment that two attackers  opened fire on a Jewish owned grocery  store now the state's attorney general  says there is growing evidence that the  motive of these shooters was hate Don  Dahler is at the scene in Jersey City  which is just across the river from  where we are in Manhattan Don what kind  of evidence do prosecutors have well  they are looking at what's being  described as a manifesto style document  that was found here at the scene as well  as a number of weapons and that new  surveillance video that shows a  completely different angle of the attack  they believe that David Andersen was  wielding an ar-15 you can see him firing  on the street before he enters the store  with the other suspect Francine Graham  right behind him with a shotgun  investigators say the shooters also had  handguns one of them with a homemade  silencer and a device to catch shell  casings in all officers say they  recovered five guns a pipe bomb and  hundreds of shell casings at the scene a  law enforcement source confirmed a  manifesto style document was also found  inside the u-haul truck that was used by  the suspects the letter was described as  a few pages and contained lists of  grievances as well as groups that were  hated the attackers killed three people  in the store and a police officer at a  cemetery about a mile away before being  killed in a gun battle with police two  of the victims Mendel Firenze and Moshe  Deutsch have been laid to rest and a  funeral will be held next week for  Jersey City police detective Joseph  seals he is a father of five the other  victim  Douglas Miguel Rodriguez will be sent  back to his home his native home in  Ecuador after a funeral on Sunday his  family tells us that he's been living in  this country for three years legally  with his wife and an 11 year old  daughter  Anthony Dunn thank you very much Don  Dahler
 

